  {
    "number": 60,
    "title": "Embed shared agent monitoring with durable ownership and remote access",
    "body": "Refs #31. Guide companion: https://github.com/jimmie-potts/agent-device-hub/pull/112.\n\nCompose released agent-state 1.0.0 inside the existing Pixoo backend. The opt-in monitor has one private durable owner, scoped credentials, bounded ingestion, the existing SSE transport, labels and notice acknowledgment. A selected embedded/remote source keeps consumers on one owner through explicit quiesce/export/import. Monitoring never calls the device writer. Preserve simulator startup as the default and the existing explicitly configured device mode, as confirmed by the owner.\n\nThe owner moved numeric performance measurement and acceptance to [hardening #61](https://github.com/jimmie-potts/divoom-app-upgrade/issues/61) on September 20. That story follows #31 and does not gate this feature or dependent feature progress. Failed receipts and frozen limits remain unchanged. Correctness, privacy, authentication, durability, bounded resources, consumer isolation and hard fail-open deadlines remain mandatory. Source delivery installs no hooks and operates no devices.\n\nRuntime validation at `ae25a76bb6c597c96e1f08b81300878932ca46b9`, unchanged in current head `77e3bb17ef83c40b3760b02bd648ee5cd09821f6`, base/merge-base `e541412b201fa9a0bfa5c10f7108ca217536691e`:\n\n- Node 24 `npm run check`: 535 application tests in 52 files, typecheck/lint, 13 current specifications, the active change and 14 archived changes, plus all 10 workflow fixtures pass. The package regression verifies the archive/manifest/file hashes and executes all 96 upstream Node tests. A separate Python run passed both tests covering the shared 36-case snapshot inventory.\n- Browser validation: all 52 tests pass on the final head.\n- Integration coverage includes authenticated admission, privacy, duplicate/prior-turn events, durable labels/notices, child uncertainty, journal bounds, actual interrupted transactions, ownership exclusion, cutover/rollback, remote acknowledgment/filter/feed parity, host loss, SSE capacity/backpressure and bounded producer/measurement failures.\n- Three complete 9,000-call measurements remain failed. The latest retained WAL/FULL run had concurrency-1 p99 up to 104.3 ms against 65 ms and concurrency-50 p99 up to 716.9 ms against 396 ms. Full results and limitations are in `docs/performance/gh-31-embedded-host.json`. These diagnostic receipts precede the controller merge; there is no passing qualification for the final head. Other host workloads were not controlled; this does not establish the cause of the misses. Harness RSS is not standalone-service qualification.\n- Independent Standards and Specification rounds resolved invalid filtered snapshots, missing loss notifications and stale-state handling after malformed remote replies. Their subsequent spawn-error cleanup finding is fixed with a passing regression. Both independent reviewers reassessed this committed head and reported no remaining code findings. Specification independently reran six monitor/native-controller event tests on the final head. Numeric acceptance is deferred to #61. Fresh independent Standards and Specification reviews of current head `77e3bb17ef83c40b3760b02bd648ee5cd09821f6` against `e541412b201fa9a0bfa5c10f7108ca217536691e` found no P0-P3 findings. Each independently passed 15 tests across five monitor suites; Specification also passed current workflow validation.\n- Required hosted checks remain all five configured jobs: Workflow Ubuntu/Windows, Application Ubuntu/Windows, and Simulator browser. Branch-protection lookup returns account-plan HTTP 403; procedural gates remain mandatory.\n\nThe controller API delivery in main was merged into this candidate. Both opt-in configurations and package pins are preserved. Browser, monitor and native-controller GET/HEAD streams now share a 16-stream admission cap, preserving capacity for ingestion. Independent review verified the merge and HEAD correction.\n\nThe first hosted Windows application job failed the new backpressure fixture because OS buffering cleared the induced pressure. The fixture now corks the actual writable stream; local checks pass. Its successor run was superseded by the HEAD correction. All five current-head jobs and their executed steps passed in [run 35532310524](https://github.com/jimmie-potts/divoom-app-upgrade/actions/runs/35532310524). No unchanged failed-job reruns were requested.\n\nGuide PR #112 merged as `ee1f4405798ea1c6645cec1f9d17b288f5feffd3`. Its merged tree matches the reviewed candidate. All guide paths satisfy both workflow exclusions; zero main runs/checks are expected and verified under the guide-only exception. Public publication was not performed.\n\nThe current head synchronizes `agent-monitor-host` and archives `gh-31-shared-monitor-host`. Node 24 `npm ci`, `npm run check:workflow` and `npm run test:workflow` pass: 14 current specifications, zero active changes, 15 archives and 10 workflow fixtures. Existing application/browser evidence remains applicable to unchanged runtime code. The performance receipt file is unchanged.\n\nRemaining delivery gates: fresh independent reviews, all five current-head CI jobs, guarded squash merge, successful merged-main checks, issue completion and guide reconciliation. A follow-up companion updates the performance deferral; source and guide delivery do not authorize public publication.\n",
    "state": "open",
